### Problem

You are given the following input data:

* An array of book objects.
* The book object contains additional information about the books.

```js
const books = [
  {
    title: "The Tempest",
    authors: ["William Shakespeare"]
  },
  {
    title: "The End of Mr. Y",
    authors: ["Susan Hill"]
  },
  {
    title: "Pride and Prejudice",
    authors: ["Jane Austen"]
  }
]
```

### Challenge

* Define a function that takes in an array of book objects as its parameter.
* The function should return an API endpoint that can retrieve the book information.

### Hint

* The API endpoint should take in the [book object](./book.js) as its parameter.
* The API endpoint should return the [book object](./book.js) as its response.
* The [book object](./book.js) should contain the following information:
  * The book's title.
  * The book's authors.
* You will need to create a new function to take in the array of book objects and return the API endpoint.

### Solution

```js
const books = [{
    title: "The Tempest",
    authors: ["William Shakespeare"]
  },
  {
    title: "The End of Mr. Y",
    authors: ["Susan Hill"]
  },
  {
    title: "Pride and Prejudice",
    authors: ["Jane Austen"]
  }
];

function bookAPI(books) {
  return (
    `/api/books?title=${books[0].title}&&authors=${books[0].authors.join(',')}&
    title=${books[1].title}&&authors=${books[1].authors.join(',')}&
    title=${books[2].title}&&authors=${books[2].authors.join(',')}`
  );
}
```

