Describe how to solve this:

Tree Queries: In this problem, you are given a tree with n nodes and a set of queries. Each query asks you to find the maximum value on the path between two nodes in the tree. You need to answer all queries efficiently.

For example, if the input is the following:

- Tree with n = 5.
- Path from node 3 to node 4 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 4 to node 5 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 5 to node 1 has the maximum value.

Then the output is 4.

Write a method to solve the queries.

For example, if you are given the input:

- Tree with n = 5.
- Path from node 1 to node 2 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 2 to node 3 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 3 to node 4 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 4 to node 5 has the maximum value.
- Path from node 5 to node 1 has the maximum value.

Then the output is 3.

An efficient solution is O(n + q), where q is the number of queries.

class Solution {
    // O(n+q) time, O(1) space
    public int maxPathSum(TreeNode root, int[] queries) {
        int res = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < queries.length; i++) {
            int[] path = new int[queries.length];

            findMaxPath(root, path, 1, 0);
            res = Math.max(res, path[queries[i] - 1]);
        }

        return res;
    }

    private void findMaxPath(TreeNode node, int[] path, int i, int j) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }

        path[j] = node.val;
        findMaxPath(node.left, path, i + 1, j);
        findMaxPath(node.right, path, i + 1, j + 1);

        if (path[j] > path[j - 1]) {
            path[j] = path[j - 1];
        }
    }
}

